{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I need to explore the workspace to understand the context before creating the sprint planning package. There are several files that might contain relevant information about the initiative.",
  "plan": "First, I'll read the existing files to understand the context: initiative.txt, epic_notes.md, stakeholders.csv, and explore the skill_context directory. This will help me create accurate sprint planning documents.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat initiative.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat epic_notes.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat stakeholders.csv\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered context about the initiative. The key information is:\n- Initiative: Self-service report export for end users and administrators\n- Goal: Allow users to export filtered reports to PDF and CSV\n- Constraints: 2-week sprint, average velocity 28, one developer at 50% PTO\n- Personas: End User (HIGH priority), Administrator (HIGH priority), Power User (MEDIUM priority)\n- Requirements: INVEST-compliant user stories, Given-When-Then acceptance criteria\n\nThe SKILL.md file was truncated. Let me read it fully to understand the templates and best practices.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file to understand the agile product owner templates and workflows, then create the three required files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file was truncated but I got useful information about user story templates, INVEST criteria, and the general workflow. I have enough context to create the sprint planning documents. Let me read more of the skill context to get the acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning details.",
  "plan": "Read more of the SKILL.md file using tail or head commands to get the remaining content, particularly the acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning sections.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -300 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The file is still being truncated. Let me try to get the rest of the SKILL.md content, particularly the acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning sections.",
  "plan": "Use tail command to see the latter part of the SKILL.md file to get acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning workflows.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -400 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md content is being truncated. Let me try to get the middle section with sed to see the acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning details.",
  "plan": "Use sed to extract specific line ranges from SKILL.md to get the acceptance criteria patterns and sprint planning sections.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '100,300p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I'm getting useful content about acceptance criteria patterns. Let me get more of the SKILL.md file to see the sprint planning section and backlog prioritization details.",
  "plan": "Use sed to extract lines 300-500 from SKILL.md to get sprint planning and backlog prioritization sections.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '300,500p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered useful information about acceptance criteria patterns, INVEST checklist, and velocity tracking. Let me get the sprint planning section from the middle of the file.",
  "plan": "Extract the sprint planning section from SKILL.md, then create the three required files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,300p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "All three files have been created successfully:\n- epic_breakdown.txt (9049 bytes) - Contains epic breakdown with personas and Given-When-Then acceptance criteria\n- prioritized_backlog.txt (11641 bytes) - Contains prioritized stories with Must/Should/Could priorities and Fibonacci story points\n- sprint_plan.txt (10216 bytes) - Contains 2-week sprint plan with velocity calculation (28 × 0.9 = 25), committed (21 pts) and stretch (4 pts) sections\n\nLet me verify the files are properly created and contain the required content.",
  "plan": "Verify the three files exist and contain the expected content by checking key sections of each file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la *.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -30 epic_breakdown.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A2 'VELOCITY' sprint_plan.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep 'Priority:' prioritized_backlog.txt | head -10\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
